A||||6||chris6878||Need Help Fast...  ||||5||
Z||000000||chris6878||10-04-2000||03:30 AM||||My car has been acting strange lately...  i will be driving down the road with no problems and it will just die on me.. and wont start back up.. i have been messing with it a few days with no luck..    but i have figure out were the source of the problem is..<P>When the car dies, i can just gently press on the distrubtor, kind of tilting it a little (with the ignition on) and then my fuel pump will kick on. Like i just turned on the ignition...  i get back in the car and then it starts fine...<P>it seems to be some type of loose connection, but what in that area could be making the fuel pump kick on when tilting the distributor.. (i may need to check and make sure everthing is tight there)   any suggestions..?<P>thanks in advanced,<BR>chris||||reg||5
Z||000001||862M4inCA||10-04-2000||04:41 AM||||Mine acted funny like that once....but it wouldn't die while I was driving. I'd drive somewhere, get out for a few minutes, and when I'd go back to try to start the car it wouldn't start, and acted like it was out of gas. Happened a few other times as well. Put a new fuel pump and injecter (the injector was replaced since I suspected that to be going out as well). Ran fine for a week until one day I was driving and it just died while I was driving. Replaced the Ignition module and pickup coil and haven't had a problem since.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Sillhouette.com||10-04-2000||07:37 AM||||Sounds like an ingnition module.  I have not heard of actully moving the distributor to fix it though.  Usually when the ignition module goes the car just dies.  <BR>There is a first time for everything.  <P>Later||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cliff Pennock||10-04-2000||08:19 AM||||Yes, it does sound like the ignition module. I would replace it anyway since it's not an expensive part at all.||||reg||1
Z||000004||StuGood||10-04-2000||01:40 PM||||Well, this one makes me think (ow!)...<P>The ignition module gets grounded (to the distributor) through its two attach screws.  What grounds the distributor?  Maybe the distributor housing itself is loosing ground  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">.  Just a thought (ow - again!)  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Carrolles||10-04-2000||03:58 PM||||According to the Helms manual for the 85 model V-6 and the L-4 the ignition module is grounded to the ECM via the blk/red wire (circuit #453) through the C506 and C509 connectors.||||reg||1
Z||000006||chris6878||10-05-2000||02:47 AM||||pickup coil and ignition module are both less than a month old if that helps.  Get this,  the car ran fine all today without any problems. I am getting ready to trade it in for a truck anyway.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">          but i still have my 85 GT that is waiting for a V8.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>thanks for the replies everyone, <BR>||||reg||3
